INSTALL directions for libstatfsext:

After unpacking the tarball or pulling from git 'cd' into the top-level directory.

From there you can type:

$ make

to build the library. Then type:

$ sudo make install

to install the library system-wide. The library is currently installed
to /usr/lib, the header file to /usr/include, and the man pages to 
/usr/share/man/man3. You can edit the PREFIX variable in the make file
to install the package to a place of your choice.

Other make targets include:

test - build the library and three small test programs

strip - strips the library of debugging symbols

debug - builds the library with debugging symbols. This also passes
		-rpath='./lib' to the linker, so you can play with the code
		directly fromm the install directory, rather than having to 
		install it to the system.

uninstall - removes all installed files. Must be root or 'sudo'.

clean - removes all object files and binaries from the source tree.


